wayland-vnc (1.0.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Quality release. This package behaves exactly as in 1.0.0: the payload, the
    systemd user unit, the default 127.0.0.1:5900 bind and the Local Network
    Access switch. The GNOME backend wayland-vnc-grd gains one fix: a session now
    follows a resize of the mirrored monitor instead of freezing on its last
    frame (GNOME Remote Desktop patch 0009).
  * A qualification campaign ran against the actual RealVNC viewers, desktop and
    Android, in KVM guests; its fixes cover the Plasma portal, GNOME monitor
    hot-plug, 4K and suspend in the guests, and a harness false pass on lock.
    No desktop is release-qualified at this version.
  * Static analysis (SonarQube Cloud) now runs beside the pinned linters, locally
    and in CI, over one shared configuration so a finding on a laptop is the
    finding CI reports. Its quality gate blocks the build.
  * Release tooling fix: the AppImage build chose its appimagetool checksum from a
    case with no default, so an unexpected architecture reached sha256sum with an
    empty checksum and the build reported a tampered tool it had never heard of.
    It now fails naming the architecture.
  * Two regular expressions in the Android qualification harness backtracked
    super-linearly; both now match in linear time.
  * The Ubuntu 26.04 base image digest every fixture and package smoke pins was
    refreshed, as was the Ubuntu cloud image the KVM qualification guests are
    built from, verified against Ubuntu's signed SHA256SUMS.

 -- ventura8 <alexandrescu.sergiu@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0300

wayland-vnc (1.0.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of the Wayland VNC server toolkit for RealVNC viewers.
  * Installs a hardened systemd *user* unit running WayVNC inside the logged-in
    Wayland session, and enables and starts it for every logged-in user. A random
    viewer password is generated on first start, so it is never unauthenticated.
  * Binds 127.0.0.1:5900, this machine only, by default. Local Network Access is
    one switch in the settings app: on, the server binds every interface and is
    reachable from every network the machine is on (a user unit cannot fence that,
    so no such claim is made); off, it is back to this machine only.
  * GTK4/libadwaita settings application, translated into 101 languages, following
    the desktop's own language by default, with diacritics-tolerant search and a
    verified right-to-left layout.
  * On GNOME, requires the VNC listener to belong to this session's daemon and
    adopts the daemon's keyring password into the stored credential. The patched
    GNOME Remote Desktop backend ships separately as wayland-vnc-grd.
  * Read-only compositor/portal/capability probing (doctor/status), provisioning
    helpers, and the published qualification schema and safety documentation.

 -- ventura8 <alexandrescu.sergiu@gmail.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0300
